    ],
    "effect_type_raw": "Healing",
    "organism_type": "unknown",
    "organism_type_basis": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan plans a strength path set with All-out Effort Gu as core and Self-reliance Gu plus Bitter Strength Gu as support.",
        "chapters": [
          286
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-set",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_all_out_effort_gu",
          "gu_bitter_strength_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He already holds the Gu when he locks that set around All-out Effort Gu, and he treats further spending as needing to go toward useful areas such as still-missing Bitter Strength Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          296
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-set",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Once he holds all three, they form a tight combination: injuries raise output while healing keeps that injured state usable. Against Ju Kai Bei he sometimes restrains the Gu so injuries stay high for Bitter Strength Gu, then activates it when fractured arms threaten combat, healing while he evades with horizontal charge Gu and vertical crash Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          318
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-set",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ju_kai_bei",
          "gu_horizontal_charge_gu",
          "gu_vertical_crash_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Broken arms can be forced back into place while the Gu regrows bone, then flesh, then skin.",
        "chapters": [
          319
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-set",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After he beats Ju Kai Bei, onlookers name the same pairing again and treat Self-reliance Gu with Bitter Strength Gu as near perfect beside Strength Qi Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          321
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "strength-path-set",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_strength_qi_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "appearance": {
    "claims": [],
    "visual_confidence": "unknown"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It stimulates metabolism so injuries recover faster as the Gu Master’s strength grows.",
        "chapters": [
          161
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "early-effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Against Zhu Ba he heals internal shock damage between assaults, then uses the Gu for potent sustainability after blade-aura wounds, stopping blood loss and growing flesh while tendons heal more slowly.",
        "chapters": [
          299
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "combat-healing",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_zhu_ba"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After he drops one boar strength and adds bull, horse, and half a turtle strength, the effect has surpassed flesh-bone Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          299
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "combat-healing",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Later fights again show him healing critical injuries with it while under pressure.",
        "chapters": [
          360
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "combat-healing",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Later the healing has far surpassed flesh-bone Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          342
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-power-over-time",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "By the San Cha Mountain stretch the same Gu is still rank three, already at peak stage, and he has no recipe to advance it. Even so, when he can display formidable strength, its healing can match rank four healing Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          345
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-power-over-time",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_san_cha_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Northern Plains the rank three Gu can only show rank two effects; after wounds close a little, that weakened heal falters further.",
        "chapters": [
          428
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-power-over-time",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_northern_plains"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "His second aperture still lists the healing Gu as rank three Self-reliance Gu among Southern Border strength Gu under region suppression.",
        "chapters": [
          504
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-power-over-time",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_southern_border",
          "gu_strength_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He later finds a rank four Self-reliance Gu among expanded alliance resources and judges he must take it, because his Southern Border copy is suppressed and he lacks the recipe to raise it himself.",
        "chapters": [
          522
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-power-over-time",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": false,
